---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../../../components/Hero.astro';
import LangSwitch from '../../../components/LangSwitch.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Terms of use of the Dragon Gems Swipe app | Ludiven Studio"
	description="Terms of use and sale of the Dragon Gems Swipe mobile game: optional account, coins and hearts, purchases, video ads, leaderboards and fair play, liability, governing law."
	lang="en"
	alternates={{ fr: '/dragons-gems/cgu/', en: '/en/dragons-gems/cgu/' }}
>
	<div class="wrapper stack gap-12 legal">
		<div class="stack gap-8">
			<LangSwitch lang="en" href="/dragons-gems/cgu/" />
			<Hero
				title="Terms of use — Dragon Gems Swipe"
				tagline="Coins for the game, and fair play on the leaderboards."
			/>
		</div>

		<p class="updated">
			<strong>Dragon Gems Swipe</strong> app (<code>com.ludivenstudio.dragonsgems</code>) — last updated:
			November 5, 2026.
		</p>
		<p class="updated">
			This is a courtesy translation. In case of discrepancy, the
			<a href="/dragons-gems/cgu/" hreflang="fr">original French version</a> prevails.
		</p>

		<div class="summary">
			<p><strong>Key points before you play:</strong></p>
			<ul>
				<li>The game is <strong>free</strong> and is played without an account. Coin packs and "Unlimited hearts" can be bought, but every level can be played without buying anything.</li>
				<li>Coins and hearts <strong>have no cash value</strong>: they cannot be traded, resold or refunded, except where the law requires it.</li>
				<li>Purchases go through <strong>Google Play or the App Store</strong>. Without an account, your progress and your coins are only on your phone: uninstalling the app erases them.</li>
				<li>On the leaderboards: <strong>no cheating, no offensive names</strong>. A name or a score that breaks these rules can be removed.</li>
			</ul>
		</div>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>1. Purpose and acceptance</h2>
			<p>
				These terms govern the use of the Dragon Gems Swipe mobile game (hereinafter "the Game") and the sale
				of its paid content. By installing or using the Game, you accept them. If you refuse them, do not use
				the Game and uninstall it.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>2. Publisher</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>Company name: <strong>Ludiven Studio</strong></li>
				<li>Legal form: EURL (French single-member limited company) with share capital of €1,000</li>
				<li>Registration: 999&nbsp;253&nbsp;586 R.C.S. Vienne — SIRET 999&nbsp;253&nbsp;586&nbsp;00013</li>
				<li>EU VAT number: FR20&nbsp;999253586</li>
				<li>Registered office: 1166 route de la Ranche, 38440 Châtonnay, France</li>
				<li>Publication director: Ludiven Studio</li>
				<li>Contact: <a href="mailto:contact@ludiven-studio.fr">contact@ludiven-studio.fr</a></li>
			</ul>
			<p>See also the <a href="/mentions-legales/">legal notice</a> (in French).</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>3. The Game</h2>
			<p>
				Dragon Gems Swipe is a puzzle game: you swipe gems to match them, blast them and open chests that fill
				the treasure of Bijou, a baby dragon. It offers levels, a daily challenge, an endless mode, a summit
				challenge, world leaderboards, a daily gift and a shop.
			</p>
			<p>
				Levels play without an account and offline. The daily challenge, the leaderboards, the online save, the
				videos and purchases need the internet. Connection and equipment costs are borne by you.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>4. Account (optional)</h2>
			<p>
				The Game is played <strong>without an account</strong>: your progress is then kept on your phone only,
				and uninstalling the app or changing phones loses it. To save it online and get it back on another
				device, you can sign in with your <strong>Google</strong> or <strong>Apple</strong> account, from
				Settings. This account is the <strong>Ludiven Studio account</strong>, which is also used by the
				Pétanque Meet app and the website.
			</p>
			<p>
				The Game is not meant for children under 13. If you are a minor, ask your parents before a purchase;
				if you are under 15, also before signing in with an account and before accepting video ads.
			</p>
			<p>
				You are responsible for what is done from your account. Keep access to your Google or Apple account:
				it is what lets you get your progress back. An account cannot be transferred or sold.
			</p>
			<p>
				You can delete your account at any time: Settings › "Delete my account". Deletion is final and also
				applies to Pétanque Meet: your online save cannot be given back. What is erased is described in the
				<a href="/en/dragons-gems/confidentialite/#suppression">privacy policy</a>.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>5. Coins and hearts</h2>
			<p>
				<strong>Coins</strong> make up Bijou's treasure. They are earned by playing or bought in packs (see
				§6), and spent in the Game, for example to continue a lost level or on a breath from Bijou.
				<strong>Hearts</strong> let you play levels; they refill over time, or come from an optional video.
			</p>
			<ul>
				<li>Coins and hearts are a <strong>personal user license</strong> within the Game. You do not own them.</li>
				<li>They <strong>have no cash value</strong>: they cannot be converted into money, traded between players, resold or refunded, except where the law requires it.</li>
				<li>Without an account, they are only on your phone and <strong>disappear if you uninstall the app</strong>. Signed in, your treasure is also kept online until you delete your account; your hearts stay on the phone.</li>
				<li>The publisher may change the coin prices, the winnings and the difficulty of the levels. Coins obtained through an error in the Game, through cheating or through a refunded purchase may be taken away.</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>6. Purchases</h2>
			<p>The Game sells, for real money:</p>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>coin packs</strong>, added to Bijou's treasure;</li>
				<li><strong>"Unlimited hearts"</strong>, a one-time, permanent purchase, with no subscription: levels no longer cost a heart.</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				The price is the one shown in the Game at the time of purchase, in your currency, including taxes. A
				price change has no effect on purchases already made.
			</p>
			<p>
				<strong>Payment goes exclusively through Google Play or the App Store</strong>, depending on your
				phone, and follows their terms. The publisher has no access to any banking data. The proof of purchase
				is issued by the store. Parental controls on purchases are those of the store.
			</p>
			<p>
				"Unlimited hearts" is tied to your Google Play or App Store account: after a reinstall, or on another
				phone linked to the same account, "Restore purchases", in the shop, gives it back. Coin packs cannot be
				restored: without a signed-in account, coins lost with the phone cannot be given back. If a purchase is
				not credited, write to us with the store's proof of purchase.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>7. Right of withdrawal and refunds</h2>
			<p>
				Coins and "Unlimited hearts" are digital content supplied immediately after purchase. In accordance
				with Article L221-28 13° of the French Consumer Code, by requesting their immediate supply, you
				<strong>waive your right of withdrawal</strong> of fourteen days, which you acknowledge at the time of
				purchase.
			</p>
			<p>
				Refunds are handled by the store where the purchase was made:
				<a href="https://support.apple.com/en-us/HT204084" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Apple</a> or
				<a href="https://support.google.com/googleplay/answer/2479637?hl=en" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Play</a>.
				We cannot refund in their place, but we can help you with the process: write to us. Your statutory
				guarantees of conformity remain in force.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>8. Advertising</h2>
			<p>
				The Game offers videos, always by your choice and a few times a day: a heart when you have none left,
				continuing a lost level, doubling your daily gift, coins in the shop. Never during the daily challenge,
				endless mode or the summit challenge. Unity's video ads (Unity Ads and ironSource Ads, through Unity
				LevelPlay) are offered only if you accepted them ("Accept", or later in Settings › "Ad choices");
				otherwise, they are videos of our other games. Unity chooses the ads: the publisher does not control
				their content and is not liable for the products or services they present. Your consent and the data
				used are described in the <a href="/en/dragons-gems/confidentialite/#publicite">privacy policy</a>
				(§6).
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>9. Leaderboards: the rules</h2>
			<p>
				The daily challenge, endless mode and summit challenge leaderboards show your name and your score to
				everyone. You agree to play fair on them:
			</p>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>no cheating</strong>: do not modify the Game, its files or its network exchanges, do not use automated tools, do not use a flaw in the Game to win coins or leaderboard points;</li>
				<li>a <strong>decent name</strong>: nothing offensive, hateful, discriminatory, sexual or promotional, not another person's name, and no surname, number or address. A filter replaces the most common offensive names with "Anonyme", but it does not catch everything;</li>
				<li>do not disrupt the service.</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				To report a name, write to <a href="mailto:contact@ludiven-studio.fr">contact@ludiven-studio.fr</a> and
				give the name.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>10. Moderation and penalties</h2>
			<p>
				The publisher may, without notice, <strong>remove or replace a name</strong> that breaks these rules,
				<strong>erase a score</strong> from the leaderboards, take away coins obtained by cheating, and
				<strong>delete an account</strong> for a serious or repeated breach. To challenge a decision, write to
				<a href="mailto:contact@ludiven-studio.fr">contact@ludiven-studio.fr</a>.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>11. Intellectual property</h2>
			<p>
				The Game, its code, its images, its animations, its sounds, its texts and its characters, including
				Bijou and Perle, belong to Ludiven Studio or its licensors and are protected by intellectual property
				law. You receive a personal, non-exclusive right of use. Components by other authors remain their
				authors', under their licenses.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>12. Changes, interruption and discontinuation of the service</h2>
			<p>
				The publisher may change the Game, add or remove features, and adjust the coin prices, the winnings
				and the difficulty of the levels. The daily challenge, the leaderboards and the online save rely on our
				server and its providers: they may be interrupted for maintenance or by an outage.
			</p>
			<p>
				The publisher may stop all or part of the service, in particular if running it is no longer viable or
				if a store requires its removal. It will then tell players in the Game, with reasonable notice. Levels
				will remain playable as long as the installed version works on your phone. Discontinuation does not
				give rise to a refund of coins or of "Unlimited hearts", except where the law requires it.
			</p>
			<p>
				These terms may change. The date of the update appears at the top of the page. In the event of a
				significant change, the Game will let you know; continuing to play means you accept them.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>13. Liability</h2>
			<p>
				The Game is provided as is. The publisher does not guarantee that it works without interruption or
				error on all phones, nor that the online services are always available.
			</p>
			<p>
				The publisher can only be held liable in the event of proven fault, and its liability is limited to
				direct and foreseeable damage. It does not cover progress kept only on the phone and lost, nor progress
				lost through the deletion of the account or the loss of access to the Google or Apple account. Nothing
				here excludes its liability in the event of gross negligence or physical injury, nor limits your
				mandatory consumer rights.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>14. Personal data</h2>
			<p>
				The processing of your data is described in the
				<a href="/en/dragons-gems/confidentialite/">Dragon Gems Swipe privacy policy</a>, which forms part of
				these terms.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>15. Governing law and disputes</h2>
			<p>
				These terms are governed by <strong>French law</strong>. If you are a consumer living in another member
				state of the European Union, you keep the mandatory protections of your country.
			</p>
			{/* TODO legal: replace with the mediator's name, address and website once adhesion is signed (art. L612-1). */}
			<p>
				If there is a problem, write to us first: we will look for an amicable solution. If there is no
				solution within one month, you can turn to a consumer mediator free of charge (Article L612-1 of the
				French Consumer Code). The mediator's contact details are given on request at
				<a href="mailto:contact@ludiven-studio.fr">contact@ludiven-studio.fr</a>. Failing agreement, the
				dispute will be brought before the competent courts.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>16. Contact</h2>
			<p>
				For any question or to report a problem:
				<a href="mailto:contact@ludiven-studio.fr">contact@ludiven-studio.fr</a>.
			</p>
		</section>
	</div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.legal {
		max-width: 68ch;
		margin-inline: auto;
		color: var(--gray-200);
		font-size: var(--text-md);
		line-height: 1.6;
	}
	.legal h2 {
		font-size: var(--text-xl);
		color: var(--gray-0);
	}
	.legal ul {
		padding-left: 1.2rem;
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 0.35rem;
	}
	.legal a {
		color: var(--accent-regular);
		text-decoration: 1px solid underline transparent;
		text-underline-offset: 0.25em;
		transition: text-decoration-color var(--theme-transition);
	}
	.legal a:hover,
	.legal a:focus {
		text-decoration-color: currentColor;
	}
	.updated {
		font-size: var(--text-sm);
		color: var(--gray-300);
	}
	.summary {
		border: 1px solid var(--gray-800);
		border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-regular);
		border-radius: 0.5rem;
		padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
		background: var(--gray-999_40);
	}
	.summary p {
		margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
	}
	code {
		font-size: 0.9em;
		background: var(--gray-999_40);
		padding: 0.1em 0.35em;
		border-radius: 0.25em;
	}
</style>
